          "title": "You'll want to know: виноватый",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "виноватый (vinovátyy) — \"guilty, to blame\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Никто не виноват, так получилось. Niktó ne vinovát, tak poluchílos. Nobody is to blame; that is how it turned out."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The short form виноват is the usual one: я виноват — it is my fault. Виноват! is also a quick apology."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "виноватый (vinovátyy) is built on вина (viná) \"guilt\" with the suffix -оватый; вина (viná) is usually traced to Proto-Slavic vina."
            }
          ]
        },
