          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "оправдание (opravdániye) — \"an excuse, a justification\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Для такого поведения нет оправдания. Dlya takógo povedéniya net opravdániya. There is no excuse for such behaviour."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Neuter. In court it means an acquittal."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "оправдание (opravdániye) is built on оправдать \"to justify\", from правда \"truth\", inherited from Proto-Slavic pravĭda, built on pravŭ \"right, correct\" (EtymDB). To justify is to show that someone was in the right."
            }
          ]
        },
